  "notes": "{虫|むし} is a broad term covering insects, bugs, and worms.\n\nCOMMON INSECT WORDS:\n- {昆虫|こんちゅう}: insect (scientific term)\n- {毛虫|けむし}: caterpillar\n- {蚊|か}: mosquito\n- {蝶|ちょう}: butterfly\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {虫歯|むしば}: cavity (tooth decay)\n- {虫眼鏡|むしめがね}: magnifying glass\n- {虫除|むしよ}け: insect repellent\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {虫|むし}がいい: selfish, asking too much\n- {虫|むし}の{知|し}らせ: premonition, gut feeling\n- {腹|はら}の{虫|むし}が{治|おさ}まらない: can't suppress one's anger",
